From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:05:41 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(tls): sniff ClientHellos fragmented across handshake
 records

From Jolymmiles/Xray-core (d3fcd37b, with 5e7bb42e and cc8ae360 in the
same file): a ClientHello carried in several TLS records, as RFC 8446,
section 5.1 allows and as DPI-bypass tools split it, was not sniffed, so
its flow lost its server name for domain routing and destOverride. The
sniffer now reads the handshake across records and waits for the rest.

The sniffer taken as it is there, with its tests and the Chrome, Firefox
and curl ClientHellos they read. Against the sniffer before, the record
tests fail: "with 100-byte records: SniffTLS() = (<nil>, not client
hello), want chrome.sniff.test".

Co-authored-by: TaiLer <tailer@localhost>
Co-authored-by: Jolymmiles <75259437+Jolymmiles@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
